me":"CJ Murray","position":{"name":"Linesman","displayName":"Linesman","id":"25"},"order":0}]},"article":{"headline":"Stamkos has goal, assist to lead Predators to 3-1 victory over Blues","description":"— Steven Stamkos had a goal and an assist and Juuse Saros made 25 saves to lead the Nashville Predators to a 3-1 victory over the St. Louis Blues on Saturday.","story":"NASHVILLE, Tenn. -- — <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5037/steven-stamkos\">Steven Stamkos</a> had a goal and an assist and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3042109/juuse-saros\">Juuse Saros</a> made 25 saves to lead the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/nsh/nashville-predators\">Nashville Predators</a> to a 3-1 victory over the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/stl/st-louis-blues\">St. Louis Blues</a> on Saturday.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4392471/ross-colton\">Ross Colton</a> and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4419638/nick-perbix\">Nick Perbix</a> also scored and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5436/roman-josi\">Roman Josi</a> had two assists for Nashville.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5080171/jimmy-snuggerud\">Jimmy Snuggerud</a> scored and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4587909/joel-hofer\">Joel Hofer</a> made 26 saves for the Blues, who have lost three straight.\n\n\r\n              Snuggerud scored the game’s first goal at 13:07 of the opening period. \n\n\r\n              With the Blues on a power play, Snuggerud beat Saros with a one-timer from the lower part of the left faceoff circle.\n\n\r\n              Snuggerud leads the Blues with nine goals this season.\n\n\r\n              Nashville, who entered Saturday with the NHL’s third-best penalty kill at 90%, had not allowed a power-play goal against in its previous seven games.\n\n\r\n              Stamkos evened the game 1-1 with 3:53 remaining in the first, also on the power play.\n\n\r\n              The power-play goal was the 248th of Stamkos’ career, giving him sole possession of fifth place in NHL history for man-advantage goals.\n\n\r\n              Colton gave Nashville a 2-1 lead at 9:02 of the second, snapping a wrist shot from the high slot over Hofer’s glove. He has scored a goal in three straight games, equaling a career high.\n\n\r\n              Josi, the Nashville captain, has five points in his past three games.\n\n\r\n              Perbix scored an empty-net goal with 1:29 remaining for his second goal in three games. \n\n\r\n              <hl2>Up next</hl2>\r\n              Blues: host Detroit Tuesday.\n\n\r\n              Predators: visit Los Angeles Tuesday. \n\n\r\n              ------\n\n\r\n              \r\n                <a href=\"https://apnews.com/hub/nhl\">See AP’s full NHL coverage here</a>","published":"2026-11-07T20:56:34Z"}}